---
// The parts of a run and what travels between them: an event comes in, Inngest keeps the state of every step, and
// it reaches your code one of two supported ways, shown side by side. Over HTTP, Inngest calls the app's endpoint and
// the app answers with a step result or the output. With Connect, the worker opens a WebSocket to Inngest, executions
// arrive over it and results go back over it. It uses the diagram classes of the guides; with five columns it needs
// more room than they do, so it lines up from 56rem.
---

<figure class="arch not-content">
  <div class="fig-flow">
    <div class="fig-node source">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7z"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Event source</p>
      <p class="detail">Your API, a webhook or a schedule</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fig-link event">
      <div class="fig-arrow forward"><span>event in</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="fig-node accent inngest">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 18h10a4 4 0 0 0 .6-7.95A6 6 0 0 0 6.2 9.2 4.4 4.4 0 0 0 7 18z"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Inngest</p>
      <p class="detail">Inngest Cloud, self-hosted or the dev server</p>
      <div class="extra store">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="7.5" ry="2.8"></ellipse><path d="M4.5 5v14c0 1.6 3.4 2.8 7.5 2.8s7.5-1.2 7.5-2.8V5"></path><path d="M4.5 12c0 1.6 3.4 2.8 7.5 2.8s7.5-1.2 7.5-2.8"></path></svg>
        <span>Step state stored by Inngest</span>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <svg class="done" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="12" height="12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5"></path></svg>
            <code>charge</code> done
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="done" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="12" height="12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5"></path></svg>
            <code>send-receipt</code> done
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mode-title http-only">Over HTTP</p>
    <div class="fig-link http http-only">
      <div class="fig-arrow forward coral"><span>POST /api/inngest</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow back plan"><span>206 · step result</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow back ok"><span>200 · done</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-node app http-only">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 9h18M6.5 6.5h.01M9.5 6.5h.01M8 14l2 2-2 2M12 18h4"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Your ASP.NET Core app</p>
      <p class="detail"><code>MapInngest</code> runs one step per call</p>
    </div>

    <p class="mode-title connect-only">Or over Connect, with no public endpoint</p>
    <div class="fig-link socket connect-only">
      <div class="fig-arrow back run"><span>WebSocket, opened by your worker</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow forward coral dashed"><span>executions over the socket</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow back ok dashed"><span>results over the socket</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-node private worker connect-only">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect><path d="M9 2v4M15 2v4M9 18v4M15 18v4M2 9h4M2 15h4M18 9h4M18 15h4"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Your Connect worker</p>
      <p class="detail">No public endpoint; runs behind a firewall</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    <span class="http-only">
      An event reaches Inngest, which starts a run. Inngest calls the app's /api/inngest endpoint; the app runs the next
      step and answers 206 with its result, which Inngest stores. When the function returns, the app answers 200 and the
      run is done.
    </span>
    <span class="connect-only">
      With Connect, your worker opens a WebSocket to Inngest and keeps it open. Executions arrive over it, the worker
      runs the next step and sends the result back over the same socket, and Inngest stores it. The worker needs no
      public endpoint, so it can run behind a firewall.
    </span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>


<style>
  .arch {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .arch > .fig-flow {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--idn-border);
    border-radius: 0.875rem;
    background-color: var(--idn-surface);
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .detail code {
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
  }


  .mode-title {
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .store {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--idn-border-strong);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    text-align: start;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .store svg {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--idn-ok);
    stroke-width: 1.7;
  }
  .store ul {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .store li svg {
    margin-inline-end: 0.3rem;
    vertical-align: -0.1em;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .store code {
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  figcaption > span {
    display: block;
  }
  figcaption > span + span {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* The row layout of the guides' diagrams, at a breakpoint of its own. Each way to reach the code is a row on the
     right; Inngest and the event source span both. */
  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .arch > .fig-flow {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(6.5rem, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(11rem, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas:
        'source event inngest http-title http-title'
        'source event inngest http app'
        'source event inngest connect-title connect-title'
        'source event inngest socket worker';
      align-items: center;
      padding: 1.75rem;
    }
    .source {
      grid-area: source;
    }
    .event {
      grid-area: event;
    }
    /* Inngest spans both ways to your code, so every arrow on its right starts at its edge. */
    .inngest {
      grid-area: inngest;
      align-self: stretch;
      justify-content: center;
      padding-block: 2rem;
    }
    .inngest .name {
      font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
    }
    .inngest .icon {
      width: 36px;
      height: 36px;
    }
    .http-only.mode-title {
      grid-area: http-title;
      padding-inline-start: 0.5rem;
    }
    .http {
      grid-area: http;
    }
    .app {
      grid-area: app;
    }
    .connect-only.mode-title {
      grid-area: connect-title;
      padding-inline-start: 0.5rem;
    }
    .socket {
      grid-area: socket;
    }
    .worker {
      grid-area: worker;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
    .app + .mode-title {
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
    }
    .fig-node {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.3rem;
      padding: 1.1rem 1rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .fig-link {
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      padding: 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .fig-arrow {
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 0 0 0.55rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .fig-arrow::before {
      inset: auto 0 0;
      width: auto;
      height: 2px;
    }
    .fig-arrow.back::before,
    .fig-arrow.dashed::before {
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, var(--arrow) 0 5px, transparent 5px 9px);
    }
    .fig-arrow::after {
      inset-inline-start: auto;
      top: auto;
      bottom: -5px;
      border-inline: 0;
      border-block: 6px solid transparent;
    }
    .fig-arrow.forward::after {
      top: auto;
      bottom: -5px;
      inset-inline-end: -1px;
      border-top: 6px solid transparent;
      border-inline-start: 8px solid var(--arrow);
    }
    .fig-arrow.back::after {
      top: auto;
      bottom: -5px;
      inset-inline-start: -1px;
      border-bottom: 6px solid transparent;
      border-inline-end: 8px solid var(--arrow);
    }
  }
</style>
